dArkOS: the clock and the battery's percent on the screen.
- UI Settings > Show Clock (DrawClock) showed no clock with es-theme-nes-box, the
  default theme, which has no clock of its own. ES puts one at the bottom right
  in the theme's help font, in a box 5% of the screen wide and 0 high, which made
  it multi-line: "00:00" is 66 px there, the box 64 at 1280x720, and
  Font::wrapText put the time on a second line, below the screen. The box now
  fits the longest time ("00:00 PM") on one line, its right edge where it was. A
  theme that places the clock itself still does.
- The battery indicator was left-aligned in a box 0.033 of the screen wide, at
  0.955: with "Show battery" as text (the default) the percent ran off the right
  edge. It is right-aligned in a wider box now, the items ending where the two
  icons did. A theme that places the indicator itself (es-theme-replica, at the
  left edge) keeps upstream's left alignment, unless it names one.

diff --git a/es-core/src/Window.cpp b/es-core/src/Window.cpp
index 5934279..95db44c 100644
--- a/es-core/src/Window.cpp
+++ b/es-core/src/Window.cpp
@@ -21,6 +21,20 @@
 #include "components/VolumeInfoComponent.h"
 #include "components/BrightnessInfoComponent.h"
 
+// dArkOS RG52 Mini: the clock's box. Upstream's is 5% of the screen wide, its right edge at
+// 99%, and 0 high, which makes it multi-line: a time wider than the box was put by
+// Font::wrapText on a second line, below the screen's bottom edge, and no clock was seen
+// (1280x720, es-theme-nes-box's help font: "00:00" is 66 px, the box 64). The box fits the
+// longest time and is one line high; its right edge stays where it was. A theme that places
+// the clock itself still does, by applyTheme after this.
+static void placeClock(const std::shared_ptr<TextComponent>& clock)
+{
+	auto font = clock->getFont();
+	float w = std::max(Renderer::getScreenWidth() * 0.05f, font->sizeText("00:00 PM").x() * 1.2f);
+	clock->setPosition(Renderer::getScreenWidth() * 0.99f - w, Renderer::getScreenHeight() * 0.9965f - font->getHeight());
+	clock->setSize(w, font->getHeight());
+}
+
 Window::Window() : mNormalizeNextUpdate(false), mFrameTimeElapsed(0), mFrameCountElapsed(0), mAverageDeltaTime(10),
   mAllowSleep(true), mSleeping(false), mTimeSinceLastInput(0), mScreenSaver(NULL), mRenderScreenSaver(false), mInfoPopup(NULL), mClockElapsed(0),
   mIgnoreKeys(false)// batocera
